WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.767
-Welcome back, everybody.
We are here with Mandy Moore.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.501
Her new album --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:09.067
Her new album, "In Real Life,"
is out on Friday.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.801
I want to quickly mention that
you sang a song on

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:13.534
"This Is Us" a few weeks ago.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:18.834
And the next day, it went to
number 1 on the iTunes chart.

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:19.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
Look at that.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:22.868
♪♪
-It's really bizarre.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:26.367
-How fun is that?
-So much fun.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.467
I mean, the power of television
is alive and real.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:30.868
Yes.
-It's real. Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:35.334
Yeah. I remember, growing up,
I loved "Family Ties,"

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:38.200
and there was this song
by Billy Vera &amp; The Beaters,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.367
"At This Moment."

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.434
That was a song that they
played, and then --

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.667
It was just a song, and then
I guess this guy, Billy Vera,

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.868
recorded it a couple years
before, and it wasn't a hit.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:47.100
Then they aired it on
"Family Ties,"

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.968
and everyone is like,
"What is that song?"

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:52.601
And it went to number 1.
-I love those stories.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:53.934
-It's the best.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.767
-Congratulations to you, bud.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.701
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:06.601
-Is "This Is Us" get you back
into music and recording?

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:09.968
-Yeah, so, that was something
that, unbeknownst to me,

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:12.167
when I got cast,
Dan Fogelman decided to make

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.367
my character's backstory
music-related,

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:16.267
and it kind of sent me
into the studio

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.901
very early on
in the first season.

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:23.000
And I remember I sang this
Little Feat-Linda Ronstadt song

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.334
called "Willin'."

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:28.100
And I had a band with me,
and I was like, "I miss this.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.234
I remember this feeling."

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.834
I hadn't made a record in,
you know,

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.200
five, six, seven years
at that point.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.834
And it activated something
in me again that --

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.701
it just pushed me
to start writing

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.033
and get into the studio
and make a record.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.133
Yeah.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.667
-Yeah. "In Real Life"
is out on Friday.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.167
-Yes, sir.
-You're going on tour.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.467
-I am!

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:48.934
-I mean, June 10th,
you're in Atlanta, in Georgia.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.501
You're at, June 15th,
Webster Hall here in New York.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:53.200
-Yeah!
-The Ryman.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.901
I saw you're in D.C.
at the 9:30 Club, June 14th.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.767
-Yeah!
-Love the 9:30 club.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.334
-Me too.
-Look at all these dates.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.367
So, this is a family affair?
-I know. A family affair.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.067
My husband, Taylor,
is in my band.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.100
My brother-in-law,
Griffin, is the drummer.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.667
Gus is coming.
-The baby's coming.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.367
This is like --
-It's a Partridge Family.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.234
-The Partridge Family.
I was going to say!

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:10.634
You guys are all on
the bus together.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.734
-Yep, we are.
-♪ Come on, get happy ♪

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:13.767
-The Gus Bus.
That's what we call it.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:16.200
-The Gus Bus.
I mean, congratulations.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.167
I mean, this is going to be fun.
This is gonna be a fun tour.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.634
-It's an adventure. We'll see.
-Yeah, no.

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.801
I mean, this is --
You're performing tonight.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:23.901
Which song are you
performing tonight?

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.067
-"In Real Life."

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:27.968
-"In Real Life" is tonight.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:30.901
-The title track.
-The title track.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.801
And you got some good pics here
of the baby on the inside.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:36.801
-Yes. Got to include
the family in there.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.234
-You got to include the family.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.200
I wrote this whole record
during the pandemic

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.901
and when I was pregnant,
so it's, like, filled with

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:46.567
songs about impending parenthood
and, you know,

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:50.000
thinking of my own childhood and
trying to make sense of

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.334
what was happening in the world.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.834
But it was very cathartic
to write it.

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.133
-I love it.

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:57.033
Mandy's album, "In Real Life,"
is out this Friday.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.033
And you can watch the final
season of "This Is Us"

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.634
Tuesdays at 9:00 p.m. on NBC.

